DIAG: ath12k: report the CMEM base and skip writes below the window

Temporary, not for upstream.

ath12k_dp_cmem_init() writes the cookie-conversion page table through
ath12k_hif_write32(). On AHB that call routes by offset:

	if (ab->ce_remap && offset < HAL_SEQ_WCSS_CMEM_OFFSET)
		iowrite32(value, ab->mem_ce + offset);
	else
		iowrite32(value, ab->mem + offset);

so anything below 0x100000 lands in the Copy Engine register window
rather than in CMEM. cmem_base comes only from the QMI capability
response (resp.dev_mem_info_valid); nothing supplies a default. If this
firmware does not report dev_mem, every PPT entry is written straight
over CE registers, which would leave the Copy Engine holding addresses
the host never chose.

Print the base and the offset range, and skip the writes when the base
is below the CMEM window, so the theory can be tested against the
procd SIGILL.

Signed-off-by: Hideo Sumi <hideo.sumi@mugops.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp.c
@@ -1563,6 +1563,16 @@
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
+	ath12k_warn(ab, "DBG: cmem type=%d base=0x%08x ce_remap=%d off=0x%x..0x%x\n",
+		    type, cmem_base, ab->ce_remap ? 1 : 0,
+		    cmem_base + ATH12K_PPT_ADDR_OFFSET(start),
+		    cmem_base + ATH12K_PPT_ADDR_OFFSET(end - 1));
+
+	if (cmem_base < HAL_SEQ_WCSS_CMEM_OFFSET) {
+		ath12k_warn(ab, "DBG: cmem base below CMEM window, SKIPPING writes\n");
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	/* Write to PPT in CMEM */
 	for (i = start; i < end; i++)
 		ath12k_hif_write32(ab, cmem_base + ATH12K_PPT_ADDR_OFFSET(i),
